# Copy to .env.local. Nothing here is a secret: the NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are
# shipped to the browser, and the rest is read at build time by next.config.ts
# and proxy.ts.
#
# In the deployed environments none of this lives in a file — every value below
# is a Vercel project-settings variable, one project per environment
# (document/runbook.md). NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the client bundle
# at build time, so editing one in the Vercel dashboard does nothing until the
# project is REDEPLOYED. The failure mode is dev quietly calling the production
# API, which looks like a CORS bug and is not one.

# Base URL of apps/server. Defaults to http://localhost:4000 when unset.
#   production   https://api.kidlearn.net
#   development  https://api.dev.kidlearn.net
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Public base URL of THIS app. Used as `metadataBase` in app/layout.tsx, so
# canonical and Open Graph URLs resolve against the environment that rendered
# them rather than against production. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
#   production   https://kidlearn.net
#   development  https://dev.kidlearn.net
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Comma-separated origins that `next/image` may load MediaAsset URLs from —
# character art, badge icons, story illustrations. A remote image from an
# unlisted host throws at render time rather than failing quietly. Both deployed
# environments set https://res.cloudinary.com. See next.config.ts.
# MEDIA_ASSET_HOSTS=https://res.cloudinary.com

# --- Deployed environments only (file 38) ------------------------------------
# Both are set in the dev Vercel project and left UNSET in production. Neither is
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, deliberately: these are build/server values, and the second is a
# credential that must never reach the client bundle.

# "true" adds `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow` to every response (next.config.ts).
# Keeps an unreviewed-content build of a children's product out of search results.
#
# BUILD TIME, despite the missing NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix: Next serialises headers()
# into .next/routes-manifest.json during `next build`, so this needs a REDEPLOY to
# take effect, not a save. Verified by building both ways and reading the manifest.
# SITE_NOINDEX=true

# `user:password` for the basic-auth gate in proxy.ts. A speed bump that keeps the
# dev site out of casual reach — not a security boundary; the boundary is that dev
# holds no production data. Note there is deliberately NO basic auth on
# api.dev.kidlearn.net: a prompt mid-OAuth-redirect breaks the sign-in flow.
#
# Unlike SITE_NOINDEX this one IS a runtime value — the proxy reads it per cold
# start and it is never inlined into a bundle, client or server. Confirmed by
# grepping a build made with it set.
# DEV_SITE_BASIC_AUTH=dev:change-me
